                         CyberWar for G-Windows                  Mechanized Warfare in the 21st Century                    Copyright 1994 by Stephen Carville This is a board game simulation of one of many terrible battles fought by  Cybernetic Battle Robots (CYBR) in the southwestern United States during the  religious wars of the early 21st century.  This battle between a 170 ton  behemoth known as the "Reaper" and a diverse force of smaller CYBR's and  human infantry near the ruins of Phoenix, Arizona eventually led to be the  final defeat of the WestX Alliance in 2022.    System Requirements:    OS9/68000:        G-Windows        300K free memory     OS9000:        G-Windows        350K Free memory Contents:  OS9/68000 systems:           readme - this file.      readme.csl - instructions for installing 'csl' and 'fpu'.        CyberWar - executable. Put this in a CMDS directory.  cyberhelp.data - data file for help function.  Must be in current data                    directory.    cyberwar.doc - game documentation. cyberwar.history - brief history of the Cybernetic Battle Robots.  OS9000 systems            readme - this file.       readme.csl - instruction fro installing 'csl' and 'fpu'.         CyberWar - executable. Put this in a CMDS directory.       cyber_game - executable. Put this in a CMDS directory.  cyber_start_win - window module. Put this in a CMDS directory.  cyber_retry_win - window module. Put this in a CMDS directory.   cyberhelp.data - data file for help function.  Must be in current data                     directory.     cyberwar.doc - game documentation.  cyberwar.history - brief history of the Cybernetic Battle Robots.  If you do not already have the C Shared Library (csl) or a Floating Point  Coproccessor on your system please read the file "readme.csl" for additional instructions.  Special thanks to Ed Gresick of Delmar Co. for his help in compiling the  OS9000 version of this program.  Re